cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: dataset
title: "GWDG GPU Node Telemetry Dataset for Observability-Aware Early Warning"
abstract: >-
  Sanitized time-series telemetry from production GPU nodes at the GWDG HPC
  infrastructure, aligned with operator-curated GPU failure incidents from
  January 2025 to February 2026. Fifty incident tables sample GPU (DCGM),
  node/OS, chassis/BMC (IPMI) and monitoring-pipeline metrics every 10 seconds
  over a 26-hour window anchored on the Slurm-detected node state transition,
  alongside a scheduler-state table covering the full observation period. The
  dataset supports reproducible research on early warning for GPU instability,
  particularly detachment-class failures whose dominant signal is structural
  observability collapse - metric disappearance, scrape degradation and
  monitoring gaps - rather than any numeric threshold.
